AB  - Emergence of smart cities accelerates living of citizens by facilitating smart services in diverse domains, viz., transportation, smart home, healthcare, environment, and many more. Development of smart cities evokes both structural and technical perspectives, which effectuates the challenges of collection, storage, processing, and analysis of enormous amounts of data. Managing and processing this massive amount of data generated from numerous sources is a complex task, requiring the services of cloud computing. The generated tasks may be latency sensitive and requiring prompt response, difficult to process over cloud data center. Edge computing has been introduced as a prominent solution for such types of applications/tasks that offered cloud services at the network edge without delay. Artificial intelligence (AI) plays a crucial role in decision making and extracts valuable insight from the collected data. Several researchers have explored the sustainable smart city concept, but most of them have focused at computing paradigms, Internet-of-Things (IoT), and AI. In this chapter, we first represent the concept of a smart city, including the role of thrust technologies, like blockchain, digital twin, computing paradigm, big data, 5G, IoT, and LLMs. Furthermore, the authors have discussed various applications of smart cities and proposed the framework for a smart city with the integration of cutting-edge technologies. In the closing section, research challenges and future work has been discussed in details, that will be as a stepping stone for the new researchers in the field.
